{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And I shall set your border from the Sea of Reeds to the sea of the Philistines.</b> The Sea of Reeds, which begins in the east of the Land of Israel, and to the sea of the Philistines, which is in the west, as it is written: ״ארם מקדם ופלשתים מאחור״ (Aram from the east and Philistines from behind)." "<b>And from the wilderness.</b> Which is in the south, in which Israel journeyed forty years." "<b>And to the River.</b> That is the Euphrates, which is in the north. Some say: מושש שנים תזרע (you shall sow [your] seed for two years) — עד כי יהיה לך למוקש — was said at the end of the last forty days. And what is written in the section of תשא — ״הנה מלאכי ילך לפניך״, and ״ושלחתי לפניך מלאך״, and ״שמור לך עד בחלב אמו״ — was said at the end of the first forty days. And here, at the end of the last days, when he was fully reconciled, he wished to conclude his words with the matter of the Sabbatical year and the festivals, the warning against cooking meat in milk, the sending of the angel, and entry into the Land — just as he did in the first forty days, except that from here onward the sections are transposed."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {2 "The phrase מושש שנים תזרע is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. עד כי יהיה לך למוקש is quoted out of context and left untranslated as it appears without its lemma. The word 'מושש' (normally 'feel/grope') is obscure here and may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:12.681326243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}